  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 2,
    "summary": "The Lord gives wisdom, knowledge, and understanding—Walk in the way of good men.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "My son, if thou wilt receive my words, and hide my commandments with thee;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "OR treasure. Prov. 4:21."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "So that thou incline thine ear unto wisdom, and apply thine heart to understanding;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "2 Ne. 16:10; 3 Ne. 19:33."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, if thou criest after knowledge, and liftest up thy voice for understanding;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If thou seekest her as silver, and searchest for her as for hid treasures;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Then shalt thou understand the fear of the Lord, and find the knowledge of God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "Alma 36:7."
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "TG Knowledge."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the Lord giveth wisdom: out of his mouth cometh knowledge and understanding.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG God, Wisdom of; Wisdom."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "TG Understanding."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He layeth up sound wisdom for the righteous: he is a buckler to them that walk uprightly.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "Ps. 91:4."
          },
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "TG Walking with God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He keepeth the paths of judgment, and preserveth the way of his saints.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Then shalt thou understand righteousness, and judgment, and equity; yea, every good path.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "2 Ne. 28:30."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When wisdom entereth into thine heart, and knowledge is pleasant unto thy soul;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Discretion shall preserve thee, understanding shall keep thee:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "TG Rashness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "To deliver thee from the way of the evil man, from the man that speaketh froward things;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Who leave the paths of uprightness, to walk in the ways of darkness;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG Walking in Darkness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Who rejoice to do evil, and delight in the frowardness of the wicked;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "OR perverseness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 27
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whose ways are crooked, and they froward in their paths:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 32
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "To deliver thee from the strange woman, even from the stranger which flattereth with her words;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "OR alien woman; unchaste women were often so called. Prov. 5:3 (3, 20). TG Adulterer."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 44
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Which forsaketh the guide of her youth, and forgetteth the covenant of her God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For her house inclineth unto death, and her paths unto the dead.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "None that go unto her return again, neither take they hold of the paths of life.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Eccl. 7:26."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "That thou mayest walk in the way of good men, and keep the paths of the righteous.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the upright shall dwell in the land, and the perfect shall remain in it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Prov. 10:30."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But the wicked shall be cut off from the earth, and the transgressors shall be rooted out of it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Ps. 52:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "proverbs3",
  "prevChapterId": "proverbs1",
  "volume": {
    "_id": "oldtestament",
    "title": "Old Testament",
    "titleShort": "OT",
    "titleOfficial": "The Old Testament"
  }
}